% ===========================================================================
% refs.bib — bibliography for the bitterfs documents
% ===========================================================================
%
% The three @article entries were fetched from doi.org rather than typed:
%
%   curl -sSL -H 'Accept: application/x-bibtex' https://doi.org/<DOI> -o entry.bib
%
% Do that instead of hand-writing them.  A transposed digit in a DOI does not
% fail — doi.org happily returns a 10KB HTML error page, and `>` saves it into
% the .bib, where it becomes an unreadable biber parse error.  Use -o, not `>`,
% and never pass -f and -s together: that combination fails SILENTLY, leaving
% an empty file.
%
% Everything is \cite'd or \nocite'd somewhere; an entry nothing refers to is
% invisible in the output, and a document that cites nothing makes biber warn
% "does not contain any citations!" and print an empty bibliography.
% ===========================================================================

